 * On an ill-formed sequence, CPython's decoder reports the *maximal valid
 * subpart* as the error and resynchronises just after it; the error handler then
 * maps each byte of that subpart to U+DC00+byte.  This is why the CESU-style
 * encoded surrogate ED A0 80 comes out as three separate escapes
 * (`\udced\udca0\udc80`) rather than one.
